{
	"_description": "Expected rows of every named keystats query on query_fixture.sql, per filter and per dialect. Derived from the legacy driver SQL before the catalogue replaced it: native rows from the macOS reader (the Windows reader returned the same rows), cli_json rows from the Linux reader with its json_quote columns decoded. Catalogue choices that change a legacy result: manifest.ergo adds the focus-latency sums (Linux legacy), manifest.kc_hold keeps the Windows/macOS aliases, manifest.system_day is the Windows query. In-process engines cut TEXT at NUL, so native rows hold the truncated text the json_quote dialect preserves. The n-gram queries are the legacy Linux statements (grouped_ngram_sql); their native rows are the same rows with the text an in-process engine cuts at NUL, and replace the legacy macOS SUM reads (census finding 7). Their filter parameter set is { table = \"ngram_chars\", where, conjunction }.",
